## Context

`/pulse` names a general health check; the skill is a testing doctor for slow,
flaky or stale gates (and the guards those tests embody). The author finds the
name broader than the task and chose `/test-doctor`, pairing it with
`/trace-doctor` as the two meta doctors (2026-10-27). A themed name is waived:
the skill is meta.

Separately, trace-doctor's velocity section ranks the slow Bash tail, which is
mostly test gates, but its only output is a ticket: it has no route to the
testing consultation whose method fits that case.

Barrier denials were checked first (trace-friction, 28 d, padme, 2026-10-27):
3,391 worktree-guard refusals, none in the last 3 days, last heavy day 10-14,
matching edd139bd (plain-git worktrees). Guard ownership stays as written:
ticket 1218 routed the live PreToolUse guard to this skill.

## Actions

- Rename `skills/pulse/` to `skills/test-doctor/`, `scripts/pulse_traces.py` to
  `scripts/gate_traces.py`, `scripts/pulse_profile.py` to `scripts/gate_profile.py`,
  their tests, the survey's `pulse:` line prefix, and every live reference.
  Closed tickets and journal entries keep their wording (history).
- Chart entries become `-test-doctor-<slug>.md`; the history search reads both
  `-test-doctor-` and the older `-pulse-` entries.
- trace-doctor's velocity section offers `/test-doctor` for a gate-dominated
  slow tail instead of ticketing it; the mention test admits trace-doctor as a
  suggester (suggest, never invoke).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No live file (outside `tickets/closed/`, `memory/journal/`) names `/pulse` or `pulse_*.py`
- [ ] Chart history search covers both slugs
- [ ] trace-doctor suggests `/test-doctor` for gate-dominated slow tails; the mention test allows exactly hunt, lair, trace-doctor
- [ ] Catalog regenerated, drift clean; `make check` passes
- [ ] Runtime skill links (Claude Code, Pi) point at `test-doctor` after merge
